  "cli_result_text": "Submitted. Summary of the divergence these files establish:\n\n**Babel side** (`babel-plugin-proposal-decorators/src/index.ts` \u2192 `transformer-legacy.ts`, plus `babel-plugin-transform-typescript/src/index.ts` and `babel-preset-typescript/src/index.ts`):\n- `index.ts` picks `legacy` (stage-2, TS-compatible) vs `2023-05`/etc. (stage-3 TC39) purely from the `legacy`/`version` option \u2014 `preset-typescript` never touches this choice; it only wires in `plugin-transform-typescript` for type stripping.\n- `transformer-legacy.ts` (Babel's legacy decorator emitter) never reads `node.typeAnnotation`/type info anywhere \u2014 it only builds `applyDecoratedDescriptor`/`initializerWarningHelper` calls from the decorator expressions themselves. Babel has **no `emitDecoratorMetadata` equivalent at all**, regardless of plugin order or `legacy: true`. `Reflect.metadata(\"design:paramtypes\", \u2026)` is simply never emitted.\n\n**SWC side** (`swc_ecma_transforms_proposal/src/decorators/{mod.rs,legacy/mod.rs,legacy/metadata.rs}`, wired from `.swcrc` in `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs`):\n- `decorators()` in `mod.rs` dispatches on `Config.legacy`; metadata emission is gated by `Config.emit_metadata`, and calling `emit_metadata: true` with `legacy: false` hits `unimplemented!()`.\n- The legacy path (`legacy/mod.rs`) runs `ParamMetadata` then, if `metadata` is set, `Metadata` (`metadata.rs`) \u2014 which walks `TsTypeAnn` on class fields/params/methods to synthesize `design:type`/`design:paramtypes`/`design:returntype` via `_ts_metadata` calls, mirroring tsc's `emitDecoratorMetadata`. Because this reads live type annotations, it must run **before** type erasure \u2014 order is baked into the pass, not user-configurable.\n- `crates/swc/src/config/mod.rs` maps `.swcrc`'s `jsc.transform.legacyDecorator` \u2192 `Config.legacy` and `jsc.transform.decoratorMetadata` \u2192 `Config.emit_metadata`.\n\n**Divergence causing the customer's bug**: Nest's DI relies on `Reflect.getMetadata('design:paramtypes', \u2026)`. Babel toolchains can never populate that (no code path emits it), so Babel-based Nest projects historically require a third-party shim (`@abraham/reflection` or `babel-plugin-transform-typescript-metadata`, whose algorithm SWC's `metadata.rs` explicitly ports, per its doc-comment link). SWC *can* replicate tsc's behavior, but only if the config sets **both** `legacyDecorator: true` **and** `decoratorMetadata: true`. If the customer's `.swcrc` set `legacyDecorator: true` but left `decoratorMetadata` at its default `false` (or unset), `Config.emit_metadata` is `false`, `Metadata` never runs, no `_ts_metadata`/`Reflect.metadata` calls are emitted, `Reflect.getMetadata` returns `undefined`, and Nest's IoC container throws reading `getMetadata` off that `undefined` \u2014 exactly the reported symptom.",
